    {
      "id": 71193,
      "name": "Spiff",
      "username": "Spiff",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-08-19T20:21:39.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>That demo video is great.&nbsp; It looks like there have been a couple of changes since the info they released with the Kickstarter:</p><ol>\n<li>Decks are played face-up (is this a new thing?&nbsp; Can't remember)</li>\n<li>There's no discard pile.&nbsp; Your cards go immediately to the bottom of your deck rather than into a discard pile.&nbsp; That means no shuffling, I assume.</li>\n<li>They changed the Energy icon (a good move).&nbsp; It's a green triangle now.</li>\n<li>In combat, multiple ships which engage an enemy designate one as the primary, with the others as secondaries which support the primary ship with bonuses or abilities.</li>\n</ol><p>It all looks very good to me, and I'm still super stoked about the game.&nbsp; One thing that's clear from watching the demo however, is that table space is going to be at a premium with this game.&nbsp; Lots of large elements with lots of cards surrounding them.&nbsp; Could be rough for people playing on their kitchen nook table.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:50:17.205Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
