      "username": "McBehrer",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/{size}/1850_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-08-21T21:34:42.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Decks are played face-up (is this a new thing?&nbsp; Can't remember)There's no discard pile.&nbsp; Your cards go immediately to the bottom of your deck rather than into a discard pile.&nbsp; That means no shuffling, I assume.They changed the Energy icon (a good move).&nbsp; It's a green triangle now.In combat, multiple ships which engage an enemy designate one as the primary, with the others as secondaries which support the primary ship with bonuses or abilities.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Yes, that is relatively new, as is the no-discard-pile thing. It just came up in the most recent build, and it wasn't even officially part of it, but an afterthought that caught on. Also, the icon is green? Darn, I was expecting yellow-orange. Curse these black-and-white playtest files!</p>",
